    "question": "A restaurant makes 40 more pizzas than hot dogs every day. If the restaurant makes 60 hot dogs every day, how many pizzas and hot dogs will it make in June?",
    "gold": "4800",
    "answer": "If the restaurant makes 60 hot dogs and 40 more pizzas than hot dogs every day, it makes 60+40 = <<60+40=100>>100 pizzas.\nThe total number of pizzas and hot dogs it makes in a day is 100+60 = <<100+60=160>>160\nIn June, with thirty days, the restaurant will make 30*160 = <<30*160=4800>>4800 pizzas and hot dogs in total.\n#### 4800"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total number of pizzas and hot dogs the restaurant will make in June, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of pizzas the restaurant makes each day.\n2. Determine the total number of days in June.\n3. Calculate the total number of pizzas and hot dogs made in June.\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the number of pizzas the restaurant makes each day.**\n\nThe restaurant makes 40 more pizzas than hot dogs every day. If the restaurant makes 60 hot dogs every day, then the number of pizzas made each day is:\n\\[ 60 + 40 = 100 \\]\n\n**Step 2: Determine the total number of days in June.**\n\nJune has 30 days.\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the total number of pizzas and hot dogs made in June.**\n\nThe total number of pizzas made in June is:\n\\[ 100 \\times 30 = 3000 \\]\n\nThe total number of hot dogs made in June is:\n\\[ 60 \\times 30 = 1800 \\]\n\nAdding these together gives the total number of pizzas and hot dogs made in June:\n\\[ 3000 + 1800 = 4800 \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of pizzas and hot dogs the restaurant will make in June is:\n\\[ \\boxed{4800} \\]",
